## What the exported data shows

Counts below are computed by the kb component from its report data. It deduplicates by
report ID before selecting reports merged into ticket 4471. Repeated export rows are
not additional people or additional reports.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

CauseTable shows how the export files reports, not the corrected issue split. Its
parser row includes the {oneDayMoves.length} desk-noted one-day/timing moves because
its classifier uses tenant, channel and form without inspecting the report body.
Those moves have their own ticket; they are not day/month swaps. The table's ownership
labels describe the original support export, not the current GitHub issues.

## Corrected split

These counts are computed from the same deduplicated export. First separate the IDs
in desk-notes.json oneDayMove; classify the remaining reports using the kb's own logic.
Each report belongs to exactly one of these tickets.

| Problem | Reports | Tracking |
